WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.301
What to carry forward.

2
00:00:01.581 --> 00:00:09.027
Read productivity claims with six questions: population, task, comparison, outcome, uncertainty, selection.

3
00:00:09.307 --> 00:00:15.173
Hold four kinds of evidence together: experiments, field studies, usage data, labor data.

4
00:00:15.453 --> 00:00:29.149
In late 2026 they agree on a pattern (real, uneven gains; verification as the bottleneck; entry-level hiring affected first; no broad displacement yet) and disagree on magnitude.

5
00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:33.888
For your own team, measure rather than survey, and re-measure as the tools change.

6
00:00:34.168 --> 00:00:41.848
Week 3 turns to the risks side: what goes wrong, how labs and governments are responding, and how to judge any claim you meet.
